markdown <<MARKDOWN
## Facilitating While Loops

Students are debugging an existing program here, not writing one from scratch, which makes this a different kind of stuck than earlier labs. The real risk: converting a for loop to a while loop while forgetting the one line that makes it ever stop.

### What's Actually Happening in This Lesson

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
    <div style="background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12px; width: 24px; height: 24px; min-width: 24px; border-radius: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">1</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>Time to 10 Million:</strong> students see a real post grow by a factor of 10 each minute, until it crosses a target, without knowing in advance how many minutes that'll take</div>
  </div>
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;">
    <div style="background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12px; width: 24px; height: 24px; min-width: 24px; border-radius: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">2</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>Going Viral in Code (Levels 1-5):</strong> students take Lesson 7's fixed-days <code>simulate</code> function and rewrite it to run until <code>views</code> reaches a target, instead of a set number of days</div>
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

### Watch for: Infinite Loops

A while loop only stops when its condition becomes false. If nothing inside the loop ever changes that condition, it never will.

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; margin: 20px 0; flex-wrap: wrap;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #FFE3CE; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #611D00; margin-bottom: 10px;">Stuck: Condition Never Changes</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #611D00; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">while views &lt; target:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;print(f"Day {day}: {views} views")</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #CCF1D0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #003F25; margin-bottom: 10px;">Strong: Updates What the Condition Checks</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #003F25; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">while views &lt; target:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;print(f"Day {day}: {views} views")<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;views = views + views * growth<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;day += 1</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;">
    <strong>&#128161; Language to borrow:</strong>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; margin-bottom: 8px;">&bull; "What is your condition actually checking? Does anything inside the loop change that value?"</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222;">&bull; "If this program ran forever, which line would you look at first?"</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #D5EFFF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-top: 20px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #06338D; line-height: 1.6;">
    <strong>&#8505; A quick fix if it happens live:</strong> most platforms let you stop a running program manually. If a student's loop hangs during class, that's a teaching moment, not a crisis, point them straight at whichever variable the condition depends on.
  </div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
